{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Oregon's trial period for decriminalizing drugs concludes on Sunday. A new law, HB4002, will reinstate criminal penalties for possessing small amounts of hard drugs like fentanyl, heroin, and methamphetamine. Individuals caught with these substances will be offered a choice: facing criminal charges or participating in a treatment program. This program involves completing a behavioral health course and a \"deflection program\" to avoid fines.\n\nThe new law defines personal-use possession as a misdemeanor, potentially leading to up to six months of jail time. It also seeks to strengthen law enforcement's ability to address drug use in public areas and imposes stricter penalties for drug sales near locations like parks. Counties are encouraged, but not required, to establish treatment options to redirect individuals from the criminal justice system towards addiction and mental health services.\n\nSupporters argue the law allows counties to tailor programs to their specific needs and available resources. However, critics express concern that this could result in a fragmented and unfair system of policies. Portland police chief Bob Day explained the stringent criteria for \"deflection,\" requiring individuals to be medically stable and without other charges or a history of violence. \n\nIf eligible, officers will contact a county dispatch line to assess eligibility and connect the individual with a mobile behavioral health team. This team has a 30-minute window to make contact. If they cannot reach the person within that timeframe, the individual will be arrested. Day emphasized the need for swift action, stating they cannot simply wait around.\n\n***\n\nP.P.S. The complexities of this situation touch upon societal issues affecting people of all age groups within the country. Access to resources and support systems is crucial. It's important to consider how these changes might impact daily activities like shopping or even simple tasks like preparing to eat. Language and communication play a significant role in navigating these challenges, and understanding different perspectives is essential.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.003800314385443926}, {"token": "'", "logprob": -0.1390695422887802}, {"token": "s", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁trial", "logprob": -0.7335942983627319}, {"token": "▁period", "logprob": -0.6178813576698303}, {"token": "▁for", "logprob": -0.1016358807682991}, {"token": "▁decriminal", "logprob": -0.006587693467736244}, {"token": "izing", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "▁drugs", "logprob": -0.1778181791305542}, {"token": "▁concludes", "logprob": -1.3156956434249878}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.3079896569252014}, {"token": "▁Sunday", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.07305022329092026}, {"token": "▁A", "logprob": -0.005099978763610125}, {"token": "▁new", "logprob": -0.03692176565527916}, {"token": "▁law", "logprob": -0.014648506417870522}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.010398730635643005}, {"token": "▁HB", "logprob": -6.23445157543756e-05}, {"token": "4", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.537788011773955e-05}, {"token": "▁will", "logprob": -0.13613960146903992}, {"token": "▁reinstate", "logprob": -0.0016181482933461666}, {"token": "▁criminal", "logprob": -5.006777428206988e-06}, {"token": "▁penalties", "logprob": -0.07036665081977844}, {"token": "▁for", "logprob": -3.707340147229843e-05}, {"token": "▁possessing", "logprob": -0.0038043521344661713}, {"token": "▁small", "logprob": -0.00012408917245920748}, {"token": "▁amounts", "logprob": -1.1368727684020996}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "▁hard", "logprob": -0.